# Git Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define branching strategy, commit conventions, and PR workflow
- Ensure clean, reviewable history and safe collaboration

## Best Practices

- **Trunk-based** with short-lived feature branches
- **Conventional Commits** for all commit messages
- **PR required** for merge to `main` and `develop`
- **Squash merge** feature branches to keep history clean
- **No direct commits** to `main`
- **Linked issues** in PR description

## Branch Strategy

```
main          → production releases
develop       → integration/staging
feat/*        → new features
fix/*         → bug fixes
chore/*       → tooling, deps, config
docs/*        → documentation only
```

## Commit Message Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]

[optional footer: Closes #123]
```

**Types**: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`

**Examples**:
- `feat(cases): add case timeline activity feed`
- `fix(billing): correct tax calculation on invoices`
- `chore(deps): upgrade prisma to 6.x`

## Coding Standards

- Commit atomic changes — one logical change per commit
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or `node_modules`
- Run `lint` and `typecheck` before push
- Keep PRs <400 lines when possible

## Folder Structure

```
.github/
├── PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
└── workflows/
```

## Naming Convention

| Item | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Feature branch | `feat/short-description` |
| Fix branch | `fix/issue-description` |
| PR title | Same as conventional commit |

## Performance Rules

- N/A

## Security Rules

- Never commit secrets — use `.env.example` with placeholders
- Pre-commit hook scans for secrets (Phase 1 setup)
- Review dependency changes carefully in PRs

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ GOOD workflow
git checkout -b feat/case-filters
git commit -m "feat(cases): add status and priority filters"
git push -u origin feat/case-filters
# Open PR → review → squash merge

# ❌ BAD
git commit -m "fix stuff"
git commit -m "WIP"  # on main
```

## Things to Avoid

- Force push to shared branches
- Large PRs mixing unrelated changes
- Committing generated files unnecessarily
- Merge commits on feature branches (rebase preferred locally)
- `--no-verify` to skip hooks

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Branch named correctly (`feat/`, `fix/`, etc.)
- [ ] Commits follow Conventional Commits
- [ ] No secrets or `.env` in diff
- [ ] PR has description, test plan, screenshots (UI)
- [ ] CI passes before requesting review
- [ ] Self-review completed
